    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#william-i-duke-of-aquitaine">William the Pious</a> in 893, the duchy was ruled from Poitiers by the counts of Poitou for nearly two centuries.</li><li>Duke William IX is the earliest troubadour whose songs survive, and the ducal courts helped create courtly love poetry.</li><li>Through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#eleanor-of-aquitaine">Eleanor of Aquitaine</a> it passed to the English crown, which held Gascony until the French victory at Castillon in 1453.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#william-i-duke-of-aquitaine">William the Pious</a>, the first duke of Aquitaine, founded the abbey of Cluny in 910; its reformed monasticism spread to hundreds of houses across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#latin">Latin</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#europe">Europe</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

